[Opening "Queen's Gambit Accepted: Alekhine Defense, Haberditz Variation"]

{Queen's Gambit Accepted: Alekhine Defense, Haberditz Variation. Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.}
1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. Nf3 a6 4. e3 b5 5. a4 Bb7 {Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.} 6. axb5 axb5 7. Rxa8 Bxa8 8. b3 ! Nf6 {The point of the whole plan. Material is level, but only one side has a target to attack.} (8... cxb3 Nbd2 b2 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. bxc4 bxc4 10. Bxc4 e6 11. O-O Bd6 ?! 12. Nc3 O-O 13. Qe2 c5 14. Rd1 cxd4 15. Nxd4 Qc7 16. h3 Rc8 17. Ncb5 Qb7 18. Nf3 Bf8 19. Nd6 Bxd6 20. Rxd6 Qc7 21. Ba3 Bxf3 22. gxf3 Nbd7 23. Bb5 Ne5 24. f4 Ng6 25. Rc6 Qb8 26. Rxc8+ Qxc8 27. Qc4 Qd8 28. Bb2 h6 29. Bxf6 Qxf6 30. Qc8+ Kh7 31. Bd3 Qh4 32. Kg2 Qf6 33. Qc5 Kg8 34. Qc8+ Nf8 35. Qc7 g6 36. Qe5 Qe7 37. Qb8 Kg7 38. Qe5+ Kh7 39. Qb8 Qc5 40. Qe5 Qa3 41. Be4 Qa4 42. Bf3 Qd7 43. Qf6 Kg8 44. h4 Qd6 45. h5 Nh7 46. Qh4 g5 47. fxg5 Nxg5 48. Qg4 f5 49. Qh4 Kf7 50. Qf4 Qc5 51. Bb7 Qb6 52. Ba8 Qd8 53. Bb7 Qe7 54. Ba8 Kf6 55. Qd4+ e5 56. Qb6+ Qe6 57. Qd8+ Kf7 58. Bd5 Qxd5+ 59. Qxd5+ Kf6 60. Qd6+ Ne6 61. f4 exf4 62. exf4 Kf7 63. Qe5 Ke7 64. Qxf5 Ng7 65. Qe5+ Kf7 66. f5 Ne8 67. Qe6+ Kf8 68. Qg6 Ke7 69. Qe6+ Kf8 70. Qxh6+ Ke7 71. Qg6 Kd8 72. h6 Nd6 73. h7 Nc4 74. Qg8+ Kc7 75. Qg7+ Kb6 76. h8=Q Kc5 77. Qh3 Ne3+ 78. Qxe3+ Kb5 79. Qgd4 Kc6 80. Qec3+ Kb7 81. Qdb4+ Ka8 {Resignation is timely: the king cannot be defended and the counterplay is one move too slow.} 82. Qca3# 1-0

[Event "Sicilian - Najdorf structures: Chapter 2"]
