[Opening "Vienna Game: Frankenstein-Dracula Variation"]

{Vienna Game: Frankenstein-Dracula Variation. A slight inaccuracy in move order — the bishop is better placed before this pawn commits.}
1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. Bc4 Nxe4 4. Nxe4 d5 5. Bb5+ c6 {Book so far. The plan is the usual one: finish development, then decide which side to open.} 6. Bd3 dxe4 7. Bxe4 Nd7 8. d3 ! Nf6 {A long think. Both continuations are playable; this one keeps more pieces on, which suits the attacker.} (8... c5 Rb1 c4 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Bf3 Bc5 10. Ne2 Bg4 11. Nc3 Qd7 ?! 12. O-O O-O 13. Ne4 Nxe4 14. dxe4 Qxd1 15. Rxd1 Be6 16. Be3 Bxe3 17. fxe3 Rfd8 18. Kf2 Kf8 19. a3 Ke7 20. Be2 f6 21. Ke1 a5 22. Rd3 g6 23. Rad1 f5 24. exf5 gxf5 25. g3 Bd5 26. c4 Be4 27. Rxd8 Rxd8 28. Rxd8 Kxd8 29. c5 Kc7 30. b4 axb4 31. axb4 b6 32. Kd2 bxc5 33. bxc5 Kd7 34. Bc4 h6 35. Bg8 Ke7 36. Bh7 Kf7 37. g4 Kf6 38. h4 Ke6 39. Kc3 Kd5 40. Kb4 Ke6 41. Ka5 Bb1 42. Kb6 fxg4 43. Bxb1 Kd5 44. Bg6 g3 45. Be8 e4 46. Bxc6+ Ke5 47. Bxe4 Kxe4 48. c6 g2 49. c7 g1=Q 50. c8=Q Qb1+ 51. Ka7 Qa2+ 52. Kb8 Qb3+ 53. Ka7 Qa3+ 54. Kb6 Qb3+ 55. Ka5 Qa3+ 56. Kb5 Qb3+ 57. Ka6 Qa3+ 58. Kb7 Qb3+ 59. Ka7 Qa3+ 60. Kb8 Qb3+ 61. Ka8 Qa3+ 62. Kb7 Qb3+ 63. Ka6 Qa3+ 64. Kb6 Qb3+ 65. Ka5 Qa3+ 66. Kb5 Qb3+ {The rest is technique, which is another way of saying it still has to be played accurately.} 67. Ka6 1/2-1/2

