[Opening "Sicilian Defense: Richter-Rauzer Variation"]

{Sicilian Defense: Richter-Rauzer Variation. Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.}
1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Nc6 {Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.} 6. Bg5 e6 7. Qd3 Bd7 8. O-O-O ! a6 {The critical moment. The pieces are as good as they are going to get; something has to happen now.} (8... Nb4 Kb1 Nxa2 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. f4 h6 10. Bh4 g5 11. fxg5 Ng4 ?! 12. Nf3 Nge5 13. Qe2 Be7 14. Kb1 hxg5 15. Bg3 Qa5 16. Qe3 O-O-O 17. Be2 Nxf3 18. Bxf3 Ne5 19. Be2 Bc6 20. Rhf1 f6 21. Qg1 Kb8 22. Bf2 Nd7 23. Bg4 f5 24. exf5 exf5 25. Bxf5 Rhf8 26. Bxd7 Rxd7 27. Bb6 Rxf1 28. Rxf1 Qe5 29. Re1 Qh8 30. Qe3 d5 31. Bd4 Qc8 32. Ne2 Bd6 33. Be5 Qc7 34. Nd4 Bxe5 35. Qxe5 Qxe5 36. Rxe5 Rf7 37. b3 g4 38. Kb2 Rh7 39. Rg5 Bd7 40. Rxd5 Bc8 41. Ne2 Rxh2 42. Nf4 Rh1 43. Rg5 Rf1 44. Nh5 Rf2 45. g3 Bf5 46. Nf4 Bxc2 47. Kc3 Bd1 48. Kd4 Rxa2 49. Nd5 Bxb3 50. Nb6 Bd1 51. Rg8+ Ka7 52. Nc8+ Kb8 53. Nb6+ Kc7 54. Nd5+ Kd6 55. Rg6+ Kd7 56. Rg7+ Kd6 57. Rg6+ Kd7 58. Rg7+ Ke6 59. Nf4+ Kf6 60. Rxb7 Ra4+ 61. Ke3 Bf3 62. Rh7 Ra3+ 63. Kd4 Ra4+ 64. Ke3 Re4+ 65. Kd3 a5 66. Rh6+ Kf7 67. Ra6 a4 68. Kc3 Rxf4 69. gxf4 g3 70. Rxa4 g2 71. Ra1 Be2 72. Rg1 Bf1 73. Kd4 Kf6 74. Ke4 Ke6 75. f5+ Kf6 76. Kf4 Kf7 77. Ke5 Ke7 78. f6+ Kf7 79. Kf5 Kf8 80. Kg6 Bd3+ 81. Kh6 Bf1 82. Kg5 Kf7 83. Kf5 Kf8 84. Ke6 Bc4+ 85. Kd6 Bf1 86. Ke5 Kf7 87. Ke4 Kxf6 88. Kf4 Ke6 89. Ke3 Kf5 90. Kf2 Kf4 91. Ke1 Kf3 92. Kd2 Kf2 93. Rxg2+ {The endgame is winning but not simple — the passed pawn needs its king, not just its rook.} Bxg2 1/2-1/2
